# MSS.OSAG_IP -- the inputs on which the translation DELIBERATELY differs from Oracle:
# migration/spec/mss.osag_ip.md clauses S-IP-008, S-IP-009, S-IP-014, S-IP-020, S-IP-023
# are "CORRECTED -- DEVIATION(ORACLE-BUG)" clauses (migration/pgsql/mss/osag_ip.FINDINGS.md).
# This scenario is EXPECTED to differ; known.diff holds the accepted difference, and
# run-diff.sh reports KNOWN when the live diff equals it. known.diff was derived by hand
# from the Oracle source (the arithmetic in the cited lines) while no Oracle container
# was reachable -- the first live run confirms or corrects it (a mismatch is reported as
# DIFF, never hidden).
ORA_USER=mss
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=Oracle-bug inputs: ip2num raises/returns fraction, num2ip keeps fraction, ipv6 partial/raising, num2ipv6 NULL/negative/fraction/overflow halves
